    "details": "# Problem Description:\n\nWhen an audio channel\\'s buffer needs to be resized, the sound(4) driver\nchecks that the buffer is not memory-mapped and then drops the channel\nlock to allocate a new buffer. An mmap(2) call on another thread can\ncomplete during this window, after which the resize path frees the\nnow-mapped buffer without rechecking.\n\n# Impact:\n\nAn unprivileged local user with access to a sound device can exploit\nthis race to trigger a use-after-free in the kernel, potentially\nescalating privileges.\n",
